    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d55">

                <pb facs="0174" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/8180</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-06T10:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 7, 3.11
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2583. Department’s 1449, February 4, 2 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d55-f1"/>
                    Subsequent to my 2544, January 31, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d55-f2"/> I
                    learned indirectly that both British and French missions suspected proposed
                    meeting. In order to keep confidence of chiefs those missions I felt it
                    necessary to inform them, in strict confidence, that unofficial meeting was to
                    take place for sole object of listening to anything he<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d55-f3"/> might have to say. They have not been informed detailed
                    results thereof. May I at least inform them that matter being discussed with
                    their Governments from Washington?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
